===Verb===
{{en-verb|++}} {{tlb|en|transitive}}

# To [[varnish#Verb|varnish]] (something) with [[japan#Noun|japan]].
#: {{cot|en|ebonize}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=1847|author=editorial staff|title=[[s:Scientific American/Series 1/Volume 3/Issue 09/Veneering Metal Plates|Veneering Metal Plates]] |journal=Scientific American |section=[[c:File:Scientific_American_-_Series_1_-_Volume_003_-_Issue_09.pdf|series 1, Volume 3, Issue 9, page 68]] |passage=He fastens his plates by fine srews in any waving or curving lines, and then '''japans''' them in all the most varied and beautiful shades. }}
#* {{RQ:Beerbohm Zuleika Dobson|passage=Piled against the wall were certain boxes of black '''japanned''' tin, which had just been sent to him from London. At any other time he would certainly not have left them unopened. For they contained his robes of the Garter.}}
#* {{RQ:Lawrence Lady Chatterley's Lover|chapter=XI|page=241|passage=Among other monstrosities in this lumber room was a largeish black '''japanned''' box, excellently and ingeniously made some sixty or seventy years ago, and fitted with every imaginable object.|footer=An {{lg|adjective}} use.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1971|author=Gwen White|title=Antique Toys And Their Background|page=183|text=A Zoetrope in the same sale fetched 26 guineas. The revolving drum, 12 inches in diameter, was black '''japanned''', on a turned wooden base, and there were many coloured strips.}}
# {{lb|en|UK|religion|slang|obsolete}} To [[ordain]] (someone).
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1826|author=George Colman|title=The Connoisseur|page=179|passage=Jack, hearing that I was in this part of the world, sent me a very hearty letter, informing me, that he had been double-'''japanned''' (as he called it) about a year ago, and was the present incumbent of &mdash; {{...}}}}

